feat(client-chart): two overlay chips — price levels and the channel

The panel could show indicator panes but had no way to put geometry on the price
pane, so structure levels and the newly built channel only ever appeared as text in
the conversation. Two chips now draw them, and both recompute with the timeframe
because the host enriches each timeframe's payload separately.

Host: enrichChart gains two geometries beside the regime snapshot —
  structure: nearest confirmed resistance/support with distance and age, plus the
    last failed break;
  channel: the regression channel's two rails as endpoint pairs, with R-squared,
    position and width. A channel is straight, so two points per rail suffice.

Client: both chips are 'overlay: true' with empty figures, so they are excluded from
paneCount and hasSeries() passes for any payload; the primitives they add ride the
existing hline/polyline draw path and therefore the existing label-lane layout, so
their captions cannot collide with annotation labels.

The channel chip tries 120 bars, then 60, then 40, and reports which one it used.
A single fixed window was wrong: the panel holds ~1000 bars, and a 120-bar
regression of copper's four-month range-then-break gives R2 0.01, so the chip read
'no channel' on markets that are trending on a shorter horizon. Measured after the
fallback: copper 1d R2 0.40 at 60 bars, copper weekly R2 0.85 at 120, oil R2 0.65,
QQQ R2 0.33 — each with its own window stated in the label.

37 test files, 580 tests.